Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["RandomInfraParallel", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"0202d14a-f47e-4b17-84e9-087538982d8f"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["RandomInfraParallel"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraParallel", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0caee71b-8188-4517-a297-417a8f0eb009"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives one parallel to ",
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] a shortest path through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " that stays at the distance ",
 StyleBox["d(p, line)", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " and cannot be prolonged at that distance \[LongDash] as a directed path \
graph.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"3658724a-fc84-4c06-84c4-2182a392a473"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["RandomInfraParallel"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraParallel", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cda86c35-7866-4004-a8ff-ab4a7ffbf6eb"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ae43b03-5be8-4829-a3ef-6df4fb44cb3d"],
 " of exactly ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " parallels or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2910b695-4dbe-4745-9711-bbea81911ceb"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"UpTo", "[", "n", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f4511e14-44ac-4e6e-a0e8-fbdbf5529f2e"],
 " gives up to ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72939084-554b-48ae-9c2b-c4334a8f16f4"],
 " gives the whole class as a pool of DAGs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"6dad520a-46b5-4340-add2-a6cbe97b2f8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The default draw is random. Seed with ",
 Cell[BoxData["SeedRandom"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f3deaaf-10ac-48e0-be0a-245d4c3638e0"],
 " to reproduce it. Give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<NextVertexFunction\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "Identity"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7faafd0c-46ea-4732-b4b2-ebc7f2ad8237"],
 " for deterministic descent. ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05111016-1e87-486a-b7bc-8a9fa773b472"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData["Automatic"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91e80389-9a83-4667-a416-9f3849159052"],
 " keeps the full enumeration without drawing."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3cc7d917-caa8-465b-a981-fb775f211d5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Write ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 " for the level set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], ":", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"l", "i", "n", "e"}], "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"l", "i", "n", "e"}], "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33958a81-8c84-49d8-8961-79336a837f7d"],
 ". A parallel to ",
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is a shortest path ",
 StyleBox["s \[Ellipsis] p \[Ellipsis] e", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] so ",
 StyleBox["d(s, e) = d(s, p) + d(p, e)", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] with every vertex in ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 ", such that no neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 " prolongs it. This reads Euclid's fifth postulate intrinsically: constant \
distance is what a metric can say about parallelism without a notion of \
direction. Inextensibility is measured inside ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 ", not in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 ", so a parallel need not be a line of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0c6e2569-f95d-4a23-9c46-7a04385877e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " is a vertex sequence, a walk graph, or a list of walk graphs, which \
spreads over its walks. Each parallel appears once, oriented so that ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " precedes ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " in canonical order."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c6ef3d53-bab8-4c44-99fc-ca60953a12e0"],

Cell["\<\
On the square grid the classical picture survives: through a vertex of a \
parallel row there is exactly one parallel to a row, and it is the row. Off a \
line that bends, the level set bends with it, and a shortest path inside it \
soon has to leave \[LongDash] the parallels are then few and short. Below, \
through a vertex at distance 2 from a line through the centre, the square \
tiling has one parallel of 10 edges beside a line of 24, the irregular mesh \
two, of 4 and 5 edges, the hexagonal tiling a single edge. A vertex with no \
neighbour in its level set has no parallel at all: the class is empty, not \
the one-vertex walk.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fe028af9-7cb5-42ca-9e88-f51a33518573"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraParallelQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraParallelQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "caf995f4-0d14-4bad-8699-4b060b0db2c2"],
 " asks a different question, and the two do not match. The predicate tests \
that two vertex sets are disjoint and at constant distance, and does not \
require either to be a shortest path. So it accepts pairs this function never \
returns \[LongDash] concentric shells, for instance, are parallel by that \
test \[LongDash] while every parallel returned here passes it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6eb4c9a3-75de-4efd-a2f9-473ab060f8dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The class is carried by a ",
 StyleBox["pool",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": one shortest path DAG per admissible pair of ends (",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 "), the ",
 StyleBox["s \[RightArrow] p", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["p \[RightArrow] e", "TI"],
 " intervals cut down to ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 " and glued at ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8e60db-a25c-4834-941e-e9946a453900"],
 " returns the pool itself \[LongDash] a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0bc831c4-5367-4c74-911a-a881a6aba460"],
 " of DAGs, a single atom giving the one DAG. A bounded count streams \
parallels off the atoms as directed path graphs, and the count-less call is \
one random parallel."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2b3c456d-45f3-453b-93f7-5501dae3a362"],

